From: fil-c-utils maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Align legacy dictionary items under Fil-C on AArch64

The legacy dictionary builder stores 12-byte dictItem values in a table and
passes them by value. The AArch64 ABI copies each value as an 8-byte chunk and
a 4-byte chunk, but the table's 12-byte stride leaves every other item only
4-byte aligned. Align dictItem to 8 bytes under Fil-C on AArch64, padding each
table entry to 16 bytes without changing its values or behavior.

--- a/lib/dictBuilder/zdict.c
+++ b/lib/dictBuilder/zdict.c
@@ -154,7 +154,11 @@ typedef struct {
     U32 pos;
     U32 length;
     U32 savings;
+#if defined(__FILC__) && defined(__aarch64__)
+} ZSTD_ALIGNED(8) dictItem;
+#else
 } dictItem;
+#endif
 
 static void ZDICT_initDictItem(dictItem* d)
 {
